   "confidence": "medium",
   "notes": "15 King's Parade. Yellow stock/gault brick (weathered buff) with white stucco dressings: 1st-floor 6-over-6 sashes with architraves and triangular pediments on consoles, 2nd-floor sashes with architraves, smaller 3rd-floor sashes; every window has a cast-iron balconette on brackets. Moulded band with end consoles below the 3rd floor (string course 11.0). Black shopfront with round-arched glazing heads and dentil cornice. Photos (2016-2021) show the 'NOA NOA' clothes shop; fascia_text uses the current OSM name Fitzbillies (colours from the photos, branding of the new tenant not seen). Large white cylindrical rainwater pipe/hopper at the south edge."
